cell 0.1.0
dip8 8 pins: DIP-8 (NE555 timer)
dip14 14 pins: DIP-14 (74HC00 quad NAND)
dip16 16 pins: DIP-16 (CD4017 decade counter)
to92 3 pins: TO-92 (2N3904 NPN transistor), heat sensitive
axial-resistor 2 pins: axial resistor, 1/4 W (10 kilohm)
axial-diode 2 pins: axial diode, DO-35 (1N4148)
radial-electrolytic 2 pins: radial electrolytic capacitor (10 uF 25 V), heat sensitive
ceramic-disc 2 pins: ceramic disc capacitor (100 nF)
led-5mm 2 pins: 5 mm LED (red), heat sensitive
battery-snap 2 pins: 9 V battery snap (9 V snap, 100 mm leads), heat sensitive

reset [circuit=NAME] -- the cell as it starts: arms home, tools in the rack, the trays filled for a circuit
tool ARM TOOL [temp=C] -- change the arm's tool at the rack
joints ARM J1 J2 J3 J4 J5 J6 [speed=N] -- move the arm to absolute joint angles, all joints arriving together
move ARM to=X,Y,Z [rpy=R,P,Y] [speed=MM/S] -- move the tool to a pose, by inverse kinematics, in a straight line
lift ARM [mm=MM] -- move the tool straight up
back ARM|STATION [mm=MM] -- move the tool straight back along its own axis, away from what it touches
grip ARM open|close [force=N] -- open or close the tweezers
pick ARM PART grasp=NAME -- approach a part, close on a grasp frame, lift it
place ARM PART at=X,Y,Z [rpy=R,P,Y] -- carry the held part to a pose
align ARM FRAME to=FRAME [gap=MM] -- bring a frame of the held part to another frame, a gap apart
release ARM PART -- open the tweezers and let the part go
clip ARM on=PIN at=MM -- clip a heatsink on a lead, between the body and the joint
touch ARM|STATION at=JOINT [dwell=S] -- put the iron's tip on a joint and hold it there
feed ARM|STATION mm=MM [rate=MM/S] -- feed solder wire into the joint the iron is on
weld ARM|STATION at=JOINT energy=J [risky=refuse|allow] -- spot weld a lap of two leads by a capacitor discharge
wire ARM awg=N mm=MM -- feed bare or enameled wire from a spool out of the nozzle
cut ARM -- cut the wire or the lead in the cutter's jaws
stage [turn=DEG] [tilt=DEG] [at=X,Y,Z] -- move the positioner: turn the stage by an angle, tilt it, move it
present FRAME|JOINT at=STATION [and=STATION] [turn=DEG] [tilt=DEG] -- move the positioner so a pin's frame or a joint is at a tool station's point
pinch PINCER on=PIN [at=MM] -- a pincer on the turntable grips a lead from the side: it holds the part there, and sinks heat
unpinch PINCER -- a pincer lets go and draws back
vise open|close -- open or close the vise on the stage
wait [s=S] [until=TARGET] [below=C] -- let time pass, or wait until a pin or joint cools
scope [pan=DEG] [tilt=DEG] [zoom=N] [focus=MM] [rotate=DEG] [aim=TARGET] -- move the microscope: pan, tilt, zoom, focus, rotate, or aim it at a target
snap [stereo=N] -- take the microscope's picture
inspect TARGET -- report a joint's gap, fillet and result, or a pin's temperature
probe PIN PIN -- measure continuity and resistance between two pins
rewind t=S -- put the cell back as it was at a time (the timeline keeps both branches)

